WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.234
-Thank you for being here.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.501
-I am so excited to be back.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.234
-I know. There's so much
I want to talk to you about.

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:07.200
First of all, congrats
on "The Bridge" right here.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.901
Your EP is out now.

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:11.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:14.467
-Why did you --
Why the title "The Bridge"?

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:16.701
-Um, I wrote these two songs

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:18.501
"The Tree"
and "Get the Hell Out of Here."

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:21.667
And I just felt like
I was leaving some things

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.567
in country music behind

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:25.400
that didn't really, like,
serve me anymore.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.234
And so it felt like calling it
"The Bridge" felt like

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:33.934
just the step to the next thing,
whatever that is, but, yeah.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:35.601
-What was the headline about,
by the way?

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.067
If you don't mind
talking about it.

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:38.634
There was some headlines like,

00:00:38.634 --> 00:00:40.467
"Maren Morris
is Leaving Country Music."

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:42.367
And I go, "No."
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:45.267
Well, I don't think it's
something you can really leave

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:47.033
because it's --
-In you.

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:49.667
-It's a music that's in me,
and that's what I grew up doing.

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:51.100
It's the music I write.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:55.467
Even if I've been sort of
genre-fluid my whole career,

00:00:55.467 --> 00:00:57.701
you can't, like,
scrub the country music out.

00:00:57.701 --> 00:01:00.267
-No.
-It was very, like, hyperbolic.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:01.767
But, you know,
headlines are different

00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:03.100
from the things
you actually say.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.501
-So you're not leaving
country music.

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:06.100
-No, no, I'm taking, like,

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.367
the good parts with me,
and all are welcome.

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:11.567
But, yeah, I just -- There were
some, you know, facets of it

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.734
that I didn't really, like,
jive with anymore.

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:15.100
-Agree with.
-Yeah.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.067
So -- No. I'm a lot happier now.
-Good for you.

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:18.300
-And -- Yeah.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.234
-I love both of these songs.

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:22.467
"The Tree." These are by
different producers, right?

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:23.734
One is Jack Antonoff.

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:26.067
-One's Greg Kurstin.
One's Jack Antonoff. Yeah.

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:28.167
-They're fanta-- And tonight
you're doing "The Tree"?

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:30.033
-I'm doing "The Tree." Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:33.601
And last night, you performed
at Bowery Ballroom?

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:35.434
-Yeah. I'm, like, kind of
hungover right now.

00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:38.400
-Oh, my God. Alright. Good.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.300
At least you enjoyed yourself.
And you're honest. Yeah.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.934
Okay. Good.
But -- But how was it?

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:45.868
-It was obviously great.

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:48.033
-Okay. Yeah. Fantastic. Good.

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:49.734
-No. It was great.
-I'm glad.

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:51.467
-Yeah. I had a lot of fun.
-Yeah.

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:53.267
-It was just --
We're doing these fan-club shows

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:54.667
in major cities

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:57.801
where we just do
these small clubs.

00:01:57.801 --> 00:02:01.033
And I did my first Bowery show
back in 2017,

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:04.234
so revisiting it last night
felt kind of like coming home.

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:06.033
But they're super-intimate,
and we do all, like,

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:08.501
the deep-cut songs that the,
like, hard-core fans love.

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:11.434
-Do you like doing
the smaller shows as well
as the giant shows?

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:14.634
Like, the same or more?
Doing the smaller ones?

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.267
-I feel like last night

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:18.200
was one of my favorite shows
of all time

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:21.200
just because -- I don't know --
it just felt so free.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.167
And we're not, like, married
to a set list.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:26.133
We're being a lot more,
like, relaxed with it.

00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:27.300
So I was like,
"Can we do one of these

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.167
once a month
just to feel like..."

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:31.601
-And tonight's show
is even more intimate.

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:33.434
-Yeah!
-Yes. That's what I'm --

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:35.200
This is what I'm talking about.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.567
Taking it down
to this beautiful studio.

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:40.000
Because, obviously,
you know how to play.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.501
You're doing giant arena shows.

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:44.234
Here's you with Taylor Swift
on the Eras Tour in Chicago.

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:45.901
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:48.033
-You do it all.

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:51.067
How long have you known Taylor?

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:54.234
-We met -- I think it was
on her Reputation Tour.

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:56.667
She was kind enough to ask me
to come out and sing my song

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:58.000
"The Middle" with her.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.000
And we were in Arlington, Texas,
at the Cowboys Stadium,

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.167
which is, like, where I'm from,
so she was nice enough

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:04.968
to, like, give me that date.

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:06.868
And so we met then.

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:09.100
And then she's just been, like,
so supportive of me

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.868
and my career over the years.

00:03:10.868 --> 00:03:13.267
And I also have --
I mean, we're the same age,

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:16.100
but looking up to her
just since I was a teenager

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.400
and watching her navigate

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.200
her country music to pop career
so gracefully.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:24.901
And just the way she treats her
fans is so kind and generous.

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:27.567
-She's kind of doing it all.
-Yeah, she's setting a high bar.

00:03:27.567 --> 00:03:30.334
And so actually, like,
there was these signs

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:33.200
on the inside of the barricades
of her stadium shows,

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.667
and it's like -- It says
basically to local security,

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:39.901
like, "Fan-friendly show.
Be kind."

00:03:39.901 --> 00:03:42.067
So even to the, like,
local security,

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:44.767
like, her team saying, like,
"Don't mess with the fans.

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:46.334
Like, they're here to have fun."

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:47.868
And everyone's
really respectful.

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:49.067
And it was like --
Oh, I love that.

00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:50.701
-Yeah, she doesn't stop.
-She's the best.

00:03:50.701 --> 00:03:52.367
-I just saw you posted --

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:53.868
It's the 10-year anniversary

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:57.000
of you moving to Nashville
to start your music career.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.567
And you have an awesome photo
of you and your mom.

00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:01.634
-Yeah, my mom's here,
actually, tonight.

00:04:01.634 --> 00:04:03.801
-Wait. Where's --
Where's mom? Where's Kellie?

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:05.167
-Where is she? She's in...

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:08.234
-There's Kell-- There's Kellie!
Hi, Kellie!

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:09.467
Mom!

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:11.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:14.734
Mom, you have to be very proud.

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:17.334
Did you always --

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:20.167
Did you always know
that she was gonna make it?

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:22.200
Yeah, yeah. You knew it.
Yeah, you knew it.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.000
See, you need a supportive mom.
Yeah.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.567
But to just go out there,
and you got your U-Haul truck.

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:29.167
You know, I was --
My senior prom,

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:31.133
I took a U-Haul truck
to the prom.

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:32.667
-Hot!
-Pretty cool. Yeah.

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.734
-Did you have a date?
-I converted the back.

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:36.667
Of course I had a date.
What are you talking about?

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:40.000
Did I have a date? Yes.
Yeah, I had a date.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.434
We converted the back to, like,
a cool kind of apartment thing.

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:45.000
-Alright. Oh, my God. Okay.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.467
-It wasn't --
No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:49.567
It's not a creepy -- No, I went
with a bunch of couples.

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:51.167
Like, three other...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:53.801
No, no, no! I didn't --
No, no, no!

00:04:53.801 --> 00:04:56.167
I didn't do -- No, no, no.
No. We were kids!

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:57.667
We were kids.
We were hanging out.

00:04:57.667 --> 00:05:00.868
And we were just -- We were
having high-school fun.

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:01.968
-Yeah.

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:03.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:04.634
-And we had a driver.

00:05:04.634 --> 00:05:05.968
No one -- Yeah.
It was all -- Anyway.

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:08.767
Anyway. Yes, I went -- Anyway.
Okay. Alright. Well...

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:11.434
-Okay.
-Well...

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:13.100
did you have fun at prom?

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.501 --> 00:05:16.234
-We're not turning this
on me now.

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:18.033
-No, we're not. Not at all.

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:20.734
Can I talk about this,
by the way, to make a pivot?

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:22.000
-Yes. Thank goodness. Yeah.
-You wrote a children's book.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.601
-I did. It's not out yet.

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:25.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:25.234 --> 00:05:26.367
Yeah.

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:28.934
-This is out April 9th.

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:31.534
-Yeah, it's a spring release,
so April 9th, it'll be out.

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:33.567
But I wrote it with
my best friend Karina Argow,

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:36.601
and she's on the road with me,
and she's a former teacher,

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:39.701
and we just -- Yeah, we want to
get kids into gardening.

00:05:39.701 --> 00:05:43.200
And my son's 3 1/2 now,
so I was going to say...

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:47.000
I've read your children's book
so many times to him.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.667
-I could tell.
You love it. Yeah.

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:51.000
-No. I love it.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.267
You were just rolling your eyes
as you were saying it.

00:05:53.267 --> 00:05:56.067
-You should know, like, as a
parent, like, children's books.

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:59.334
Like, if they have a favorite,
you read it just ad nauseam.

00:05:59.334 --> 00:06:01.000
-Oh, yeah.
-And yours is incredible.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.701
-We had to get rid
of "Goodnight Moon"

00:06:02.701 --> 00:06:05.534
because I go, "That's it.
We have to just get it
out of the house.

00:06:05.534 --> 00:06:07.634
I've read it a thousand times."
-Yeah, it's like --

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:09.801
-It's a great book.
I had to get rid of it. Yeah.

00:06:09.801 --> 00:06:12.167
-Yeah, but, no, we love yours.
We have all of them.

00:06:12.167 --> 00:06:14.400
But I was just --
Yeah, I don't know.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:17.234
I was gonna ask you --
what was it like sort of --

00:06:17.234 --> 00:06:19.634
Well, obviously being a parent
and writing something,

00:06:19.634 --> 00:06:21.868
but also being able
to give this thing back

00:06:21.868 --> 00:06:24.400
to your maybe, like,
inner child?

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.367
-Yeah. Interesting.
That's -- You know,

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:29.868
I did mine
just as a total joke at first

00:06:29.868 --> 00:06:33.968
because I was like, "Well,
I want my baby to say 'dada.'"

00:06:33.968 --> 00:06:35.567
And I didn't care
how she learned

00:06:35.567 --> 00:06:37.467
how to say "dada"
as long as she said it.

00:06:37.467 --> 00:06:39.467
So I would, like,
give her a bottle of milk

00:06:39.467 --> 00:06:40.767
and I'd be like, "Dada?"
-Yeah.

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:42.400
-You know, I didn't care
if she got it wrong, you know?

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:43.701
So -- And it didn't work.

00:06:43.701 --> 00:06:45.567
And so I wrote the book
just trying to --

00:06:45.567 --> 00:06:47.267
But I did it kind of as a joke.

00:06:47.267 --> 00:06:49.467
And then it took off,
and I saw kids reading it.

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:51.300
Wait till you see that part.
-Okay.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.567
-It's going to blow your mind.
-I'll cry.

00:06:53.567 --> 00:06:55.234
-Yes. It's the next level
of something

00:06:55.234 --> 00:06:56.801
you didn't even think
was possible.

00:06:56.801 --> 00:06:59.467
And you go -- Kids are reading
your book back to you.

00:06:59.467 --> 00:07:01.434
And it's like, oh --
It's bigger than you think.

00:07:01.434 --> 00:07:03.501
And it's the most rewarding,
coolest thing ever.

00:07:03.501 --> 00:07:04.567
-Oh, my gosh.
-Congratulations.

00:07:04.567 --> 00:07:06.567
-Thank you. I'm so excited.

00:07:06.567 --> 00:07:08.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:08.901 --> 00:07:12.300
-You're performing for us
tonight with two special guests.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:14.334
-Yeah, my really good friends

00:07:14.334 --> 00:07:15.701
Mickey Guyton
and Brittney Spencer

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:18.067
are singing with me and --
-Yes! Come on!

00:07:18.067 --> 00:07:19.334
I'm excited about this.

00:07:19.334 --> 00:07:21.300
You're performing "The Tree,"

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.334
and this is the TV debut
of the song.

00:07:23.334 --> 00:07:26.100
Congratulations on "The Bridge."
Maren Morris, everyone.

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.767
The Bridge" is out now.

00:07:27.767 --> 00:07:30.267
Maren is performing for us
after the break.

00:07:30.267 --> 00:07:32.968
Stick around! Come right back!
Get ready!

